{
  "$schemaVersion": 1,
  "$description": "Legacy-derived drum fill pattern bank — a faithful port of FillGeneratorClass._addSmallFill / _addMediumFill / _addBigFill (casperaki2-engine-js). Each category (smallFill / mediumFill / bigFill) splits into an `edm` style branch (genre in {edm,brightPop,schlager} — legacy `[ 'edm','brightPop','schlager' ].includes(parameters.style)`) and a `default` (non-EDM) branch. Each branch is a weighted pool of variants; a variant is an ordered list of steps. A `step` is either an `add` (always overlay one chosen lane/grid) or a `choice` (legacy `Tools.selectRandomly([0..count-1])` — apply the matched case's adds, or nothing). `lanes`/`grids` arrays are uniform `selectRandomly` pools. `composeFrom` first composes a randomly-picked variant from that category's named pool (legacy `expandMiddleFill` = mediumFill + a fill intro). Grids are legacy verbatim 32nd-note ASCII (8 slots/beat; spaces are beat separators, stripped before overlay). A grid is overlaid at slot (4 + beat) * 8 — legacy `_addHits` with bar=1 and a negative `beat` (=4+beat); a grid that runs past slot 32 grows the lane string exactly as legacy does (e.g. the EDM clap beat:-1 cases).",
